# Cloudflare Pages — URL redirects + proxying rules
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# ADR-29 WD1 deploys the frontend to Cloudflare Pages and the
# backend to Fly.io. The frontend's `const API = ""` (see
# index.html) posts to relative paths (`/check`,
# `/annotate-lines`, `/type-of`); for this to work in
# production the same origin must serve both.
#
# Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` can proxy same-domain paths
# but NOT cross-origin paths. Choose one of:
#
# (a) Custom-domain co-hosting via Cloudflare Workers /
#     Rules:
#       - Set up a custom domain on the Pages project.
#       - Add a Cloudflare Rule (Workers, Load Balancer, or
#         Page Rules) routing `/check`, `/annotate*`,
#         `/type-of` to the Fly.io app's host.
#     This file stays empty.
#
# (b) Cross-origin (frontend on `<app>.pages.dev`, backend
#     on `<app>.fly.dev`): set the frontend's `API` constant
#     to the absolute backend URL (e.g. via a `<meta>` tag
#     read in index.html, or a build-time replacement). The
#     backend already serves the right CORS preflight (see
#     `playground/backend/lib/playground/app.rb`'s
#     `CORS_HEADERS`).
#
# The recommended path is (a) — keeps `API = ""` simple and
# preserves first-party request semantics.
